        </p>

        <h2>3. Image Conversion Results</h2>
        <p>
          Our image conversion tools are designed to produce accurate format
          conversions. However, please be aware of the following:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Lossy to lossless conversion</strong> — Converting a JPG (lossy) file to PNG (lossless) will not recover data lost during the original JPG compression. The output PNG will contain exactly the same visual information as the original JPG, with no quality improvement.</li>
          <li><strong>File size differences</strong> — Converting between formats may significantly increase or decrease file sizes. PNG files are typically larger than JPG equivalents.</li>
          <li><strong>Transparency</strong> — JPG files do not support transparency. Converting a JPG to PNG will not add a transparent background to your image.</li>
          <li><strong>Metadata</strong> — Some image metadata (EXIF data, GPS coordinates, camera information) may be stripped or altered during conversion.</li>
          <li><strong>Browser compatibility</strong> — Conversion results may vary slightly depending on your browser and device.</li>
        </ul>

